# OPEN, a probe of what the translator does today and not a norm: the other
# side of unit_named_actual_held_header_names_limit_probe. make3 declares its
# result as fn: (int: p; int: q) int and returns f3, whose own formals are x
# and y. The call h3(y: 2; x: 1), by the names f3 actually has, is refused:
# the binding takes the names of the declared header, and a Frame whose head
# is none of them is an actual by place, here a call of an unknown y.
fn: make3 (int: n) fn: (int: p; int: q) int
    fn: f3 (int: x; int: y) int
        return: n + x * 10 + y
    return: f3
h3: make3 200
int: r h3(y: 2; x: 1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
